from pathlib import Path
import json
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
old=json.loads((ROOT/'docs/stage_metadata.json').read_text())+json.loads((ROOT/'docs/bridge_metadata.json').read_text())
stages=[{'stage':x['n'],'title':x['title']} for x in old]+[{'stage':x['stage'],'title':x['title']} for x in json.loads((ROOT/'docs/v5/stage_metadata.json').read_text())]
# Each guide has a specific transfer target; an observational table is not forced
# to stand in for absent physical fields, calibrated coordinates, or raw images.
G=[
('wdbc','Rows, features and labels','Count 569 measured summaries and 30 input features. The normalized table has two extra columns: row_id and label. Explain why shape (569,32) is not a 32-feature model. Compare with transport: 840 stored rows become 210 decision examples.','Load the table, select all columns except row_id and label, and print both shapes. List what one prediction refers to before running a classifier.','The response distinguishes storage shape from model-input shape and does not call each alternative an independent traveler.'),
('wine','Linear algebra describes the array, not the domain','A thirteen-dimensional measurement vector is not an abstract mystery: it is thirteen scalar measurements in a fixed order. A matrix collects these row vectors. Columns can be correlated, repeated or expressed on different scales. Algebraic rank is not the same as a proven physical dimension of the system.','Take the first three chemistry columns of training data, calculate their means and centered matrix, then append a duplicate column. Compare matrix rank with the number of columns. Preserve the distinction between real-valued rank here and finite-field rank used later in homology.','Explain what dependence means, why duplicated measurements add no new physical observation, and why a finite sample rank is not a manifold-identification theorem.'),
('wine','A distance depends on scale','Use two wine measurements and calculate Euclidean distance by hand in two selected coordinates. Now multiply just one coordinate by 1000. This imitates a unit change, not a new physical sample. The raw distance changes. Standardizing with frozen training statistics creates another declared metric, not the uniquely correct metric.','Compare three nearest reference rows before and after an intentional feature rescaling using only the training set. Use the original metric lesson to check triangle inequality on an exact control rather than infer a theorem from numerical examples.','Identify the chosen features, units or unknown units, fitted scale and reference rows. A label code must not be included as a numerical measurement.'),
('wdbc','Projection can erase information','Taking two coordinates of a thirty-feature image summary is a projection. It is continuous as a Euclidean linear map, but it is generally not injective on the ambient space. Distinct vectors can agree in the two displayed coordinates. A pretty scatter plot therefore does not establish homeomorphism with the original feature space.','Construct vectors [1,2,3] and [1,2,9]. Show they project to the same first-two-coordinate point. Then inspect a training-only two-feature WDBC plot and state the weaker question it actually answers.','Give the exact collision example, define continuity and homeomorphism separately, and avoid inferring a clinical class boundary from a projection alone.'),
('wine','Symmetry is a declared equivalence','Reordering the rows of a point cloud does not change its set of pairwise distances. A rotation applied to all Euclidean coordinates also preserves distances. However, rotating arbitrary chemistry features mixes quantities with different meanings; it is a mathematical control, not an experimentally valid change of wine.','Permute a fixed small standardized training cloud and compare its sorted MST edge lengths. Work the square-symmetry group example in the original stage, then explain which symmetries are physically meaningful for the application.','Distinguish an algebraic invariance test from a scientific invariance assumption. Homotopy and homeomorphism are not interchangeable.'),
('wdbc','Combinatorial objects need a clear construction','The WDBC table contains measurements extracted from images; it does not contain the pixels needed to construct a cell-image cubical complex. Use the inherited handwritten-digit lab for actual pixel geometry. Use the WDBC table only as a point cloud after a metric is chosen.','Build an unfilled triangular boundary and a filled triangle by listing their simplices. Explain why the extra face changes the complex even though the visible vertices and edges can look similar. Identify which actual data source supplies pixels in the original course.','Never manufacture a 2-D image by reshaping thirty unordered features and call its holes cell morphology. State the data-to-complex rule and face closure.'),
('wine','H0 connects observations; H1 needs faces','For a small chemistry cloud, finite H0 lifetimes can be checked through the minimum spanning tree. For H1, including only graph edges is insufficient: triangles can make cycles into boundaries. Work over the declared field F2, where addition is modulo two.','Use six fixed training points to construct a Rips filtration. Compute boundary matrices on the exact triangle example from Stage 06. Explain a cycle that becomes a boundary after its face is added.','State H_k = kernel(boundary_k) / image(boundary_k+1), prove boundary-of-boundary is zero on a simplex, and do not substitute a real matrix-rank routine for finite-field elimination.'),
('wine','Filtration scale is not chronological time','A Rips threshold in standardized chemistry space is a distance. A CO2 window has a chronological time index. Both may index constructions, but they do not mean the same thing. An alpha filtration may use squared-radius values rather than the edge threshold used by this course.','Write down the Rips membership rule before reading a diagram. On the unit square, determine exactly when edges and triangles enter. Record scale convention and maximum simplex dimension in the experiment record.','Explain Rips versus Cech using pairwise distances versus a common ball intersection. Do not compare raw alpha coordinates to edge thresholds without converting conventions.'),
('co2','Persistence follows classes, not just separate counts','A barcode records how classes continue across a nested sequence. It is more than a list of Betti numbers at unrelated scales. The delayed CO2 training cloud yields a descriptor of selected windows, not a proof of an atmospheric mechanism.','Derive the square interval [1,sqrt(2)) by hand, then inspect the saved finite bars for the real training delay cloud. Identify birth, death and essential H0. Explain what a truncation endpoint would mean.','Describe the inclusion-induced maps conceptually and avoid labeling a class immortal merely because the calculation stopped.'),
('stackloss','Independent calculation catches algorithm mistakes','Twenty-one process records are small enough for independently checking H0 merge distances against a graph algorithm. The agreement tests the numerical construction, not plant physics. Keep zero-distance duplicate observations distinct at input so their zero-length merge is handled explicitly.','Run the MST-versus-persistence test on a tiny exact cloud, then on the fixed process training rows. Trace a small boundary reduction without using the reference implementation as your only authority.','Identify face-before-coface ordering, pivots, zero-length policy, essential classes and the need for (k+1)-simplices to kill k-dimensional classes.'),
('wine','Stability and scientific importance are different','Multiplying all distances by two scales barcode coordinates. Arbitrary changes in metric or reference selection are a different experiment, not an application of a fixed-filtration perturbation theorem. A long interval may still reflect a sampling artifact or a design choice.','Perturb a training-only fixed cloud by a declared bounded coordinate error, preserve point identities, and record the resulting diagrams. State which stability theorem could apply and its hypotheses before comparing numbers.','Do not apply a sublevel-function sup-norm bound to an unrelated preprocessing change. Explain deterministic robustness separately from statistical significance and usefulness.'),
('wine','A descriptor must be deployable for a new query','The case uses separate training reference rows and supervised fitting rows. Each query plus its eight neighbors generates six descriptors. The raw-only, topological-only and combined models use the same supervised fitting rows and the same test examples.','Reproduce the saved comparison, then identify every fitted component: feature scaler, reference selection, topology scaler and classifier. Explain why using test rows as landmarks would change the evaluation.','Report both successes and failures relative to the baseline. A cohort-level diagram must not be copied across rows and treated as an independent individual feature.'),
('modechoice','Defend a complete experiment','Transfer the topology-course evaluation discipline to an unfamiliar industry. The transport example makes observation-unit errors visible: four stored rows can belong to a single decision. A good report needs more than a model score.','Write an experiment contract before running the transport notebook: question, information set, grouping, split, transforms, baseline, metrics, assumptions, limits. Then compare it to the executable protocol and saved predictions.','The report is reproducible and the claim matches the unit and split. An actual-book audit remains open until the text itself is checked.'),
('co2','A cloud is not automatically a smooth manifold','Delay coordinates may make a scalar time series look like a curve or loop. To call it a smooth manifold requires local structure and smooth coordinate transitions, not a visual impression. The chart examples in the original stage provide exact objects where the assumptions can be checked.','Work the sphere-chart round trip and derivative check in Stage 13 first. Then write why a noisy observed CO2 delay cloud is not evidence of a globally verified atlas.','Distinguish an exact chart construction, sampled approximate geometry and a learned latent representation. State where smoothness and invertibility are assumed rather than measured.'),
('nile','Coordinates and physical units are part of a transform','Use the original camera/rotation lab for actual SO(3) and SE(3) calculations; a one-dimensional annual river series does not supply camera poses. The industry transfer is discipline about representation: converting a volume unit changes coordinates, not the physical amount.','Convert an annual source volume from 10^8 m^3 to m^3. Separately compose a camera-to-world transform and its inverse in Stage 14, checking multiplication order and rotation validity.','Never replace a rigid transform with feature standardization, or infer a camera chart from arbitrary measurements. Explain the distinction between coordinate change and perspective projection.'),
('nile','Calibration and denominators determine physical claims','The inherited stereo images and reference disparity are the measured geometry example. Their principal-point correction is not optional algebraic decoration. The Nile case supplies a parallel unit lesson: annual volume cannot be presented as instantaneous discharge.','Reproduce the stereo reference comparison from Stage 15 and its deliberately incorrect uncorrected-depth result. Write down each denominator and unit, then derive the unit needed to turn annual volume into an average rate.','State the measurement reference, independent evaluation locations and units. Do not describe reference-derived geometry as an independent physical measurement of the user’s cameras.'),
('wdbc','Model input type matters','VGGT uses images; a WDBC row contains already-extracted scalar features. Neither the model name nor attention makes these data interchangeable. The original attention demonstrations are exact teaching calculations; trained VGGT inference remains separately marked as not executed.','Draw the input/output contract for one image-based geometry model and for the thirty-feature classifier. Identify dimensions, units, coordinate frame, uncertainty, checkpoint and reference evidence.','Explain frame/global attention at the appropriate level while refusing to call synthetic contract arrays trained-model predictions. An unsupported data modality requires a new justified model, not reshaping the array.'),
('wine','Fit transformations on references; evaluate elsewhere','Registering geometry and standardizing feature space are different operations, but both have a fit/evaluate boundary. A transformation fitted to an evaluation target can make performance look artificially good. Wine reference rows make that boundary visible in a small setting.','Check that anchor rows and supervised fitting rows are disjoint. Then revisit similarity registration in Stage 17 and use separate fit and evaluation points. Explain why a scale gauge must be fixed before metre-valued errors make sense.','No test reference is used to fit its own transformation. Predicted shape, registered shape and independently measured shape remain distinct.'),
('co2','Fast processing must preserve time and missingness','Optimizing a data conversion can change array layout or drop rows. A faster notebook is not an improvement if weekly time gaps become invisible. Throughput and end-to-end latency are also different quantities.','Profile a vectorized calculation and a simple loop on identical finite inputs. Assert equal outputs, preserve original indices and missingness, and report the boundary being timed. Compare with the inherited queue-age experiment.','Report measured CPU timings as CPU timings, not GPU throughput or full live-system latency. Explain how batching can improve throughput while worsening result age.'),
('modechoice','Availability precedes causal or event interpretation','A choice label is available after a traveler selects a mode. A release label in sports may need future frames for offline confirmation. Using these outcomes as live inputs would be leakage. The transport case turns this abstract rule into visible excluded columns.','List the earliest availability of each transport feature; identify psize as tied to the chosen mode in the source description. Separately distinguish onset time and confirmation time in the inherited event lab.','A predicted proximity event is not verified contact, and a choice classifier does not prove a price intervention effect. Report what was observed versus inferred.'),
('wdbc','Cross-domain transfer needs a new evidence contract','The independent spatial capstone is not completed by succeeding on a medical feature table. Use this contrast to practice identifying what must change across modalities: grouping, reference standards, sensors, error units and risk.','Compare a WDBC classifier contract with a calibrated static-scene reconstruction contract. Identify at least five nontransferable assumptions and one reusable engineering check such as hashes or split integrity.','Your report distinguishes reusable method from domain validation. No medical, sports, robotic or industrial deployment is certified by a course notebook.'),
('nile','Dimensional analysis comes before an ODE fit','A finite difference of annual volume divided by years has units of volume per year per change in the indexed year; be precise about what signal is differentiated. It is not automatically the river’s instantaneous flow. Real data can identify only what its sampling and measured variables constrain.','Use known irregular timestamps to calculate difference quotients. Then list the state variables and forcing missing from the annual river table before proposing any differential equation.','State units on both sides of an equation and show at least two plausible mechanisms compatible with the same sparse observations. Do not hide non-identifiability behind a low residual.'),
('co2','An exact flow is not every discrete predictor','The local diffeomorphism material uses assumptions about smooth vector fields and existence intervals. A trained next-value regression on a scalar series need not be invertible or define such a flow. Seasonal forcing and missing state also matter.','Work the exact forward/inverse flow and finite-time blow-up controls in Stage 22. Compare their contracts with the one-step CO2 model, specifying which premises are not supplied by observations.','Keep existence, uniqueness, invertibility and numerical reversibility separate. A learned map is not a diffeomorphism merely because it has an attention layer or low prediction error.'),
('stackloss','Mechanics assumptions should not be imported blindly','The manufacturing process is an open, driven system in this small observational record. It should not be silently replaced by the conservative oscillator used to teach Hamiltonian networks. The restricted LNN example in the core is not a general learned Lagrangian.','Derive Hamilton’s equations for the exact oscillator and identify canonical momentum. Then explain why three operating covariates and one loss reading cannot identify that Hamiltonian for a real plant.','State the Legendre-transform regularity assumptions and distinguish the manufactured training experiment from observed plant dynamics. No new HNN or LNN is trained on this tiny plant table.'),
('elnino','Symplecticity is not exact energy conservation','The original source’s broad conservation claims remain attributed in the source audit. Our harmonic-oscillator counterexample is a mathematical calculation. Neither that calculation nor an observed SST series establishes arbitrary-horizon physical climate fidelity.','Recalculate the symplectic-Euler step from q=1,p=0,h=0.2: q_new=0.96,p_new=-0.2 gives energy0.4808, not0.5. Compare the symplectic condition with energy, phase and rollout errors separately.','Explain why exact continuous conservation, symplectic integration and exact numerical energy preservation are different properties. Do not label an SST forecasting model a Hamiltonian climate solver.'),
('modechoice','A normalized output is one constraint, not physical validation','Transport probabilities sum to one, an algebraic simplex constraint. That does not ensure population calibration or causal validity. Similarly, a correction using a linearized nonlinear constraint may leave residual error.','Check the sum of the four predicted probabilities. Separately reproduce the nonlinear projection residual from Stage 25 and explain why one update differs from an exact retraction or a converged constrained solve.','State exactly which constraint is satisfied and which claims remain unsupported. Normalization, nonnegativity, conservation, geodesic motion and stability are not interchangeable.'),
('stackloss','Physics residuals require defensible equations','A PINN needs a specified equation, boundary/initial conditions, coordinates and unit scales. None is supplied merely by a table having temperature and flow columns. The original Poisson PINN is a known-answer manufactured experiment; the plant case is observed regression.','Compare the analytic Poisson reference, finite-difference baseline and trained PINN in Stage 26. Then write the additional measurements and governing assumptions required before making the plant experiment physics-informed.','A low PDE residual does not establish the right PDE for the real system, and a small fit error cannot replace parameter identifiability or independent boundary validation.'),
('stackloss','Gradient surgery cannot correct an invalid physical problem','The supplied post discusses conflicts among residual, boundary and interface objectives and reports results on its benchmarks. Those claims are preserved as source claims. The course’s gradient calculations and incompatible-objective controls are not a reproduction of the full paper.','Compute a conflicting pair of gradients by hand, apply the declared projection convention and compare with the core implementation. List what the twenty-one-row plant dataset lacks for recreating a multi-domain PDE benchmark.','Separate an optimizer operation from a theorem about convergence and from empirical improvement. Wrong interface conditions remain wrong after gradient normalization.'),
('elnino','Functions-to-functions learning needs function-level examples','A regional scalar SST record can create many windows but not independent solution fields with different initial conditions. The optional Well catalogue is a different data role: numerical simulations. It is not bundled or empirically evaluated in this release.','Reproduce the small manufactured DeepONet/FNO heat examples. Then design a split by entire simulated trajectory/condition, not neighboring frames, and distinguish it from the observed SST chronological split.','State input function, output function, domain, discretization, units, solver provenance and independent split. Do not call a window classifier an operator benchmark.'),
('nile','Differentiable does not mean identifiable','A differentiable simulator supplies derivatives of its own computations. Those derivatives can be accurate while the model or parameters remain incompatible with a real river. Scalar annual observations may not distinguish several parameter combinations.','Verify the manufactured damping sensitivity from Stage 29. Next write a hypothetical two-parameter water model and explain what extra observations could distinguish parameters rather than simply fit the same annual totals.','Check gradients numerically and check scientific assumptions independently. A differentiable calculation does not provide missing sensors, causal structure or uncertainty calibration.'),
('wine','Finish with a new locked investigation, not a higher exposed score','The final scientific capstone should transfer the learning cycle to a new question and appropriately licensed data. The eight case notebooks are worked examples, so their displayed test partitions are already exposed. Reusing those as untouched benchmarks would undo the lesson.','Choose one optional dataset only after reading its card and license. Define the independent unit, metric or physical model, preprocessing fit boundary, baseline and acceptance criteria before looking at the protected outcomes. Record a hypothesis that could fail.','Provide reproducible artifacts and explicitly distinguish reproduced source results, your new measurements, mathematical reasoning and untested proposals. Keep the actual-book audit and external physical validation visibly open.')]
assert len(G)==31
index='# A transfer guide for every existing stage\n\nThese are parallel applications, not thirty-one new prerequisites. Read the original lesson first. A guide can explain why a real dataset is **insufficient** for a concept; it does not fabricate missing geometry or physics.\n\n| Stage | Topic | Cross-industry guide | Primary case |\n|---|---|---|---|\n'
for s,(case,focus,explain,task,gate) in zip(stages,G):
    n=s['stage']
    text=f'''# Stage {n:02d} transfer guide — {focus}\n\n[Original stage learning section](../../stages/{n:02d}/README.md) · [Worked case](../lessons/{case}.md) · [Dataset card](../cards/{case}.md)\n\n## Start at the right level\n\nThis guide extends **{s['title']}**; it does not replace the stage's definitions, proofs, exact controls or exercises. Read the [beginner data primer](../../docs/v6/BEGINNER_DATA_PRIMER.md) whenever the distinction between a row, feature, group or fitted parameter is unclear. The inherited stage includes the appropriate runnable core lab.\n\n## Connect the concept carefully\n\n{explain}\n\n## Your guided experiment\n\n{task}\n\nBefore running code, write a concrete prediction. After running, record the actual input rows, transforms and output. When using a manufactured control, label it as such. When using observed measurements, preserve units and metadata limitations from the data card.\n\n## Check understanding, not only execution\n\n{gate}\n\n## Evidence and continuation\n\nSave `my_work/stage_{n:02d}_transfer.md` with your prediction, hand calculation, executed notebook path, explanation and one non-supported conclusion. Preserve your existing stage progress; the new industry log is separate and does not mark this stage complete. Return later and explain the key distinction without reopening the answer. Then follow the original course to the next unassessed stage or choose one case where it answers your current question.\n'''
    (ROOT/f'industry/stage_guides/{n:02d}.md').write_text(text)
    index+=f'| {n:02d} | {s["title"]} | [{focus}](../../industry/stage_guides/{n:02d}.md) | [{case}](../../industry/lessons/{case}.md) |\n'
(ROOT/'docs/v6/STAGE_MAP.md').write_text(index)
(ROOT/'docs/v6/stage_transfer.json').write_text(json.dumps([dict(**s,case=g[0],focus=g[1],guide=f'industry/stage_guides/{s["stage"]:02d}.md') for s,g in zip(stages,G)],indent=2))
print('Created',len(G),'stage-specific transfer guides')
